Subject: [PATCH] v4l2m2m: cancel both native queues at discontinuity

Native decoder abort marks OUTPUT and CAPTURE with VB2 queue_error.
Stopping OUTPUT alone does not clear the CAPTURE error, so a flush before
LAST/EOS can leave the new epoch permanently returning EIO. Cancel and
restart native CAPTURE as well, using the existing AVAILABLE-only requeue
path so externally referenced decoded frames keep their ownership.
Non-native decoder behavior is unchanged.

--- a/libavcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec.c
@@ -1651,10 +1651,12 @@
     h264_field_pair_free(priv);
 #endif
 
-    // Clear a pending EOS
-    if (ff_v4l2_ctx_eos(capture)) {
-        // Arguably we could delay this but this is easy and doesn't require
-        // thought or extra vars
+    // Native abort marks both VB2 queues in error. Cancel both queues even
+    // without LAST/EOS, or CAPTURE keeps returning EIO after OUTPUT restarts.
+    // STREAMON requeues only AVAILABLE buffers; downstream-held surfaces keep
+    // their references and cannot be reused by the new decoder epoch.
+    if (ff_v4l2_ctx_eos(capture) ||
+        ((s->quirks & FF_V4L2_QUIRK_EXPLICIT_DRAIN) && capture->streamon)) {
         ff_v4l2_context_set_status(capture, VIDIOC_STREAMOFF);
         ff_v4l2_context_set_status(capture, VIDIOC_STREAMON);
     }
